    "translation": "I am the same toward all beings. There is none hateful to me, none dear. But those who worship me with devotion are in me, and I too am in them."
  },
  "30": {
    "words": [
      { "sa": "api", "en": "even" },
      { "sa": "cet", "en": "if" },
      { "sa": "su-durācāraḥ", "en": "one of very bad conduct" },
      { "sa": "bhajate", "en": "worships" },
      { "sa": "mām", "en": "me" },
      { "sa": "ananya-bhāk", "en": "devoted to no other" },
      { "sa": "sādhuḥ", "en": "good" },
      { "sa": "eva", "en": "indeed" },
      { "sa": "saḥ", "en": "he" },
      { "sa": "mantavyaḥ", "en": "to be thought of" },
      { "sa": "samyak", "en": "rightly" },
      { "sa": "vyavasitaḥ", "en": "resolved" },
      { "sa": "hi", "en": "for" },
      { "sa": "saḥ", "en": "he" }
    ],
    "translation": "Even if one of very bad conduct worships me, devoted to no other, he is to be thought of as good indeed, for he is rightly resolved."
  },
  "31": {
    "words": [
      { "sa": "kṣipram", "en": "quickly" },
      { "sa": "bhavati", "en": "he becomes" },
      { "sa": "dharma-ātmā", "en": "one whose self is dharma", "term": "dharma" },
      { "sa": "śaśvat", "en": "everlasting" },
      { "sa": "śāntim", "en": "peace", "term": "shanti" },
      { "sa": "nigacchati", "en": "he reaches" },
      { "sa": "kaunteya", "en": "O son of Kuntī" },
      { "sa": "pratijānīhi", "en": "declare" },
      { "sa": "na", "en": "not" },
      { "sa": "me", "en": "my" },
      { "sa": "bhaktaḥ", "en": "devotee" },
      { "sa": "praṇaśyati", "en": "perishes" }
    ],
    "translation": "Quickly he becomes one whose self is dharma, and he reaches everlasting peace. O son of Kuntī, declare: my devotee does not perish.",
    "notes": ["\"Declare\" can also be read as \"know for certain\"."]
  },
  "32": {
    "words": [
      { "sa": "mām", "en": "in me" },
      { "sa": "hi", "en": "for" },
      { "sa": "pārtha", "en": "O son of Pṛthā" },
      { "sa": "vyapāśritya", "en": "having taken refuge" },
      { "sa": "ye", "en": "who" },
      { "sa": "api", "en": "even" },
      { "sa": "syuḥ", "en": "they may be" },
      { "sa": "pāpa-yonayaḥ", "en": "of evil birth" },
      { "sa": "striyaḥ", "en": "women" },
      { "sa": "vaiśyāḥ", "en": "merchants" },
      { "sa": "tathā", "en": "and also" },
      { "sa": "śūdrāḥ", "en": "servants" },
      { "sa": "te", "en": "they" },
      { "sa": "api", "en": "too" },
      { "sa": "yānti", "en": "they go" },
      { "sa": "parām", "en": "highest" },
      { "sa": "gatim", "en": "to the goal" }
    ],
    "translation": "For having taken refuge in me, O son of Pṛthā, even those who may be of evil birth, women, merchants and also servants, they too go to the highest goal.",
    "notes": ["\"Those who may be of evil birth, women, merchants and also servants\" can be read as one group described by the three names that follow, or as four separate groups, with those of evil birth standing apart from the women, merchants and servants."]
  },
  "33": {
    "words": [
      { "sa": "kim", "en": "how much" },
      { "sa": "punaḥ", "en": "more then" },
      { "sa": "brāhmaṇāḥ", "en": "brahmins" },
      { "sa": "puṇyāḥ", "en": "pure" },
      { "sa": "bhaktāḥ", "en": "devoted" },
      { "sa": "rāja-ṛṣayaḥ", "en": "royal seers" },
      { "sa": "tathā", "en": "and also" },
      { "sa": "anityam", "en": "impermanent" },
      { "sa": "asukham", "en": "joyless" },
      { "sa": "lokam", "en": "world" },
      { "sa": "imam", "en": "this" },
      { "sa": "prāpya", "en": "having come to" },
      { "sa": "bhajasva", "en": "worship" },
      { "sa": "mām", "en": "me" }
    ],
    "translation": "How much more then the pure brahmins, and also the devoted royal seers. Having come to this impermanent, joyless world, worship me."
  },
  "34": {
    "words": [
      { "sa": "mat-manāḥ", "en": "with the mind on me", "term": "manas" },
      { "sa": "bhava", "en": "be" },
      { "sa": "mat-bhaktaḥ", "en": "devoted to me" },
      { "sa": "mat-yājī", "en": "sacrificing to me" },
      { "sa": "mām", "en": "to me" },
      { "sa": "namaskuru", "en": "bow" },
      { "sa": "mām", "en": "to me" },
      { "sa": "eva", "en": "alone" },
      { "sa": "eṣyasi", "en": "you will come" },
      { "sa": "yuktvā", "en": "having joined", "term": "yoga" },
      { "sa": "evam", "en": "thus" },
      { "sa": "ātmānam", "en": "the self", "term": "atman" },
      { "sa": "mat-parāyaṇaḥ", "en": "having me as the highest goal" }
    ],
    "translation": "Be with the mind on me, devoted to me, sacrificing to me. Bow to me. Having thus joined the self, having me as the highest goal, you will come to me alone."
  }
}
